body:
Thanks @Chakrygin 
The `max_score` is filled if you set `track_scores` in the request:

`````
POST http://localhost:9200/test/test/_search
{
    "track_scores": true,
     "query" : {
		"multi_match" : {
			"fields" : "name",
			"query" : "one"
		}
	},
	
	"collapse" : {
		"field" : "id",
		"inner_hits" : {
			"name" : "some_name"
		}
	}
}
``````

Though we should always return `max_score` when the sort is based on relevancy like the standard search does. I'll work on a patch.
